Library     taf.rfrl.procedures.resources.python.webui.webui                                    WITH NAME  webui
Library     taf.rfrl.procedures.resources.python.connections                                    WITH NAME  connections
Library     taf.rfrl.procedures.resources.python.admin_info_model.admin_info_model              WITH NAME  admin_info_model

Resource    taf/rfrl/procedures/resources/robot/RfDiagnostic.robot


*** Keywords ***
General_SiSo_Auto_RF_Statistics_Diagnostic
    [Documentation]
    ...  The purpose of the test is to check if the RF Statistics Diagnostic procedure works properly.
    ...  The procedure can be found via WEBEM: Diagnostic -> RF Diagnostic Test -> RF Statistics Diagnostic Test Result
    ...  (Additionally Test Setup tab).
    ...  If custom_rmod_list is not configured, then RF Statistics Diagnostic procedure will be performed and validated
    ...  for every RMOD from current configuration.
    ...  Main steps of the test case look like:
    ...    1) getting rmods list from configuration if custom is not provided
    ...    2) getting rmods protocol dictionary from configuration
    ...    3) configuring Statistics Diagnostic Test in Test Setup tab with "All radios" option
    ...    4) starting Statistics Diagnostic Test
    ...    5) getting and validating Statistics Diagnostic Test result for every required radio
    ...
    ...  ARGS:
    ...  :param list of int custom_rmod_list: (Optional) :
    ...         List of configuration rmod indexes for which RF Statistics Diagnostic procedure will be validated
    ...         Default value: None
    [Arguments]                                             ${custom_rmod_list}=${None}
    [Timeout]                                               24 hours

    ${bts_type}                                             hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    ${connection}                                           connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}
    Create admin session with default alias                 bts_type=${bts_type}

    ${webui_obj}                                            Create Selenium Session
    ...                                                     admin_connection=${connection}
    ...                                                     download_dir=${logs_path}
    ...                                                     bts_type=${bts_type}

    ${rmod_ids}=                                            Run Keyword if      """${custom_rmod_list}"""!='None'
    ...                                                     Set variable
    ...                                                     ${custom_rmod_list}
    ...                                                     ELSE
    ...                                                     admin_info_model.get_rmod_indexes
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}
    ${rmods_protocol}=                                      admin_info_model.get_rmods_protocols
    ...                                                     connection=${connection}

    Configure Statistics Diagnostic Test

    Start Statistics Diagnostic Test

    FOR    ${rmod_id}    IN    @{rmod_ids}
        Robot Log Operation                                 Getting RMOD-${rmod_id} results for statistics diagnostic test...
        ${rmod_statistics_result}=                          Get Statistics Test Information
        ...                                                 rmod_id=${rmod_id}
        Robot Log Operation                                 Validating RMOD-${rmod_id} results for statistics diagnostic test...
        Validate Statistics Test Result                     rmod_statistics_result=${rmod_statistics_result}
        ...                                                 rmod_id=${rmod_id}
        ...                                                 rmods_protocol=${rmods_protocol}
        Robot Log Operation                                 Verification for RMOD-${rmod_id} completed.
    END
